WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:04.430
Next question is about Joe Biden, Donald Trump
and Utah.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:10.269
David, if Mitt Romney endorses Biden, could
Biden win Utah?

00:00:10.269 --> 00:00:11.940
So the answer is no.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.259
The short answer is no.

00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:17.970
And the background for the question I understand
there was recently a poll that showed in very,

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:23.870
very right wing conservative Utah, Donald
Trump winning only by three points.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:29.130
The idea about Mitt Romney is Mitt Romney
is a Republican senator from Utah.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.170
Mitt Romney's Mormon.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.170
Utah has a big Mormon population.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:36.660
Mormons maybe what while disproportionately
Republican voters, they also may just follow

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.970
what Mitt Romney does.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.739
If Mitt Romney says, hey, vote for Biden.

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:44.400
Could it turn Utah against Donald Trump?

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.431
I don't I don't see it.

00:00:45.431 --> 00:00:50.660
I think the best case scenario would be if
Mitt Romney does endorse Joe Biden.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:55.250
That it makes Utah so competitive that Trump
has to spend money there.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:59.070
And then that means there's less money Trump
can spend in other places.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:08.290
But the truth is that since the year 2000,
the only Democrat to carry more than 30 percent

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:11.950
even in Utah was Obama in 2008.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:17.820
And he still lost like in other words, Democrats
often don't even get 30 in Utah.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:22.369
And when Obama did, he still lost very, very
significantly.

00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:29.950
The best we can hope for is that Mitt Romney
makes it a fight for Donald Trump.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.900
And now there is one other thing to think
about here.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:40.340
Imagine if Mitt Romney ran third party that
actually could take away enough from Trump

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:46.840
and Utah that it could play spoiler essentially,
and turn it over to Joe Biden.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:51.080
But the problem is that if Mitt Romney ran
third party, he'd be running third party.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:56.520
I don't think he would just run in Utah and
he would risk in places like Michigan and

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:02.760
Wisconsin and others giving the election potentially,
potentially to Donald Trump.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:03.760
We just don't know.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.909
It would be dicey and I would be worried about
it.

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:12.140
So I think the best thing job a Mitt Romney
can do is seems unlikely he's going to support

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.300
Donald Trump.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:17.200
If he is going to support Joe Biden, just
say it.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.750
And I think that that is all we can really
hope for and make Utah a fight, make Trump

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:23.760
spend some money.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.060
You know, we talk about what's going on with
Amy Magrath and Mitch McConnell in that Senate

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.560
race in Kentucky.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:33.209
I, I it's possible Amy McGrath could win.

00:02:33.209 --> 00:02:34.910
It's an uphill battle.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:38.330
In a recent poll, she was up one, but with
a huge number of undecideds and people not

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.420
yet really paying that much attention.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:41.450
I hope she wins.

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:45.810
But even if she doesn't, if it's this close,
Republicans will probably have to funnel a

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:52.200
bunch of national money into Kentucky to defend
a seat that has historically been very, very

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.050
safe for Republicans.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:56.470
That's still good, even if you don't end up
winning the seat.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:57.780
So that's my take right now.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.989
I don't think there's any real way that Joe
Biden wins Utah.

00:03:00.989 --> 00:03:02.140
But let's make a Trump fight for it.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:02.209
Why not?

